course: dictionary
lesson: 13567
title: Living and not living
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inanimate means not alive. A rock, a chair or a toy is inanimate, because it cannot grow, breathe or feel. «The rock on the beach is inanimate.» A rock never eats or moves on its own, so the word fits.
explain: Look at the word parts for clues. The prefix in- can mean not, and animate is close to alive, so inanimate means not alive. «The robot was inanimate until the lightning struck it.» Before the lightning, the robot was not alive. Always ask: can this thing breathe, grow or feel? If not, it is inanimate.
explain: Inanimate can also describe something that is still and shows no sign of life. «The puppet lay inanimate on the shelf.» The puppet is not moving and shows no life, so it is not alive. Use your check: swap in "not alive" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Inanimate means not alive.
fact: «Inanimate» is an adjective, and it describes things like «an inanimate object».
fact: In science lessons, living things are sorted from inanimate objects.
fact: In grammar, inanimate nouns name things, not people or animals, such as «table» or «stone».
fact: «Inanimate» can also mean still and showing no sign of life.
exercise: Which of these is inanimate? | A singing bird | A sleeping cat | *A wooden chair | A growing tree
exercise: «The stone on the path is inanimate.» What does inanimate mean here? | Shiny and new | *Not alive | Very large | Able to move quickly
exercise: In science, what do we sort into living and inanimate? | Plants and animals | *Objects like rocks and chairs | Words in a book | People only
test: «The statue stood inanimate in the square.» What does inanimate mean? | Very tall | Freshly painted | Full of happy sounds | *Not alive, like stone
test: Is a toy car inanimate? | No, because it has wheels | No, because it can drive | *Yes, because it is not alive | Yes, because it is red
exam: Which word means not alive? | Breathing | Lively | Animate | *Inanimate
